Keep the score vector the sampling loop already computes.

sample() walks 500 diffusion timesteps, computes a per-node score at each one,
measures an AUC against the labels and keeps only np.max over the 500. GraFlag
publishes the scores a method computed rather than recomputing them, so the
vector behind the reported number has to survive the loop.

Stored on self rather than widened into the return tuple, so the call site in
forward() is untouched.

Nothing about what the method computes changes. The selection rule is still
upstream's -- argmax over the AUCs it printed, measured against the test
labels -- and README.md says plainly what that means for the published number.

